# harness.env.example — copy to harness.env and edit, then run ./setup.sh
# harness.env is gitignored; never commit your real values.
#
# Every key is optional. hooks/_harness-env.sh reads harness.env, then
# harness.local.env from the same directory (also gitignored) for per-machine
# overrides: keep what is shared here and what differs between, say, a WSL machine
# and a Git Bash machine in each machine's harness.local.env.
#
# Both files are bash. ${WIN_HOME} is your Windows profile directory
# (C:\Users\<you>); it is worked out before either file is read, so paths under
# your profile need no user name.

# Interpreter.
# Windows path to your AutoHotkey v2 binary. Empty means auto-detect: Program Files
# AutoHotkey\v2, then %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\AutoHotkey\v2, then AutoHotkey64.exe on
# PATH. The path as the shell sees it (AHK_BIN_WSL, also AHK_BIN_SH) is derived.
AHK_BIN_WIN=""
# AHK_BIN_WIN="${WIN_HOME}\AppData\Local\Programs\AutoHotkey\v2\AutoHotkey64.exe"
# AHK_BIN_WIN="${WIN_HOME}\Documents\AutoHotkey\bin\AutoHotkey64.exe"
# 1 only if your build supports `check /Diag=json` (the +Console fork). Stock AHK: leave 0.
AHK_DIAG_JSON=0

# Project.
# PROJECT_DIR defaults to the project Claude Code opened (else the harness root).
# PROJECT_DIR="${WIN_HOME}\Documents\MyScripts"
MAIN_SCRIPT="main.ahk"                       # entry script re-validated when a dependency is edited
DEPENDENCY_SCRIPTS=""                         # comma-sep extra files that trigger a main-script recheck
NO_RUNTIME_CHECK=""                           # comma-sep persistent scripts to skip the runtime probe
NO_AUTO_RELOAD=""                             # comma-sep library modules to never auto-restart
RUNTIME_PROBE=1                               # 1 = briefly run standalone scripts to catch runtime errors; 0 = syntax-check only
# DEMO_DIR defaults to <project>\Demo; set it to save demo scripts elsewhere.
# DEMO_DIR="${WIN_HOME}\Documents\MyScripts\Demo"

# Git identity guard (opt-in; OFF by default).
GIT_GUARD_ENABLED=0
GIT_ALLOWED_IDENTITY=""
GIT_BLOCKLIST=""                              # comma-sep account names to block on push

# Hook runtime (rarely needed).
# The hooks parse their input with jq; without it they use the bundled jqlite on
# Python 3.8+. HARNESS_PYTHON pins the interpreter for that ("none" disables it).
# HARNESS_PYTHON="${WIN_HOME}\AppData\Local\Programs\Python\Python312\python.exe"
